## Ontology editor: "Name" labels renamed to "ID"

Context: entity and relationship identifiers are the local names used to build URIs (`base_uri + name`). The editor labelled them "Name", which hid that they drive the URI. Renamed the user-facing wording to "ID" in the ontology editor. Stored data keys (`name`, `uri`) are unchanged. URI rewrite on rename (DC-E06 duplicate URIs) is NOT part of this entry and is still pending.

Changes:
1. `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js`: entity field label "Icon and name" → "Icon and ID"; entity and relationship label placeholders "Defaults to name if empty" → "Defaults to ID if empty"; attribute placeholder/aria-label "Attribute name" → "Attribute ID"; relationship field label "Name" → "ID"; validation and duplicate messages now say "ID" (e.g. "An entity with ID \"x\" already exists").
2. `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-information.js`: four "Imported Entities/Relationships" table headers "Name" → "ID".
3. `src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_import.html`: conflict table header "Name" → "ID".
4. `docs/user-guide.md`: "Edit the entity/relationship name" → "ID".
5. `docs/architecture.md`: entity and relationship table rows "Name" → "ID".

