## Ontology: renaming an entity or relationship re-derives its URI (DC-E06)

Context: Sanity Check DC-E06 ("URI ... is used by 2 propertys: assignedto2, assignedto"). The editor keeps the URI on rename so mappings stay identifiable, but the freed name was then reused by a new item whose URI (`base_uri + name`) collided with the renamed item's old URI. Decision (option A): a rename rewrites the URI from the new name and remaps the mappings that reference it.

Changes:
1. `src/back/objects/ontology/ClassModel.py`: new `_rederive_renamed_uris` and `rewrite_renamed_uris`. An item is renamed when its URI was owned in the previous state by a different name; its URI becomes `<namespace><new name>` (namespace kept, so imported entities keep their source namespace). Attributes are re-derived too. Legacy duplicate URIs are ambiguous: the renamed item gets its new URI and the mappings stay on the original one. New `attribute_uris` returns attribute URIs per class (positional).
2. `src/back/objects/ontology/Editor.py`: `save_ontology_config_from_editor` re-derives renamed URIs before the orphan prune, then calls the new public `remap_mapping_uris` (entity `ontology_class`/`class_uri`; relationship `property`, `source_class`, `target_class`). The response now returns `uri_renames` (`classes`, `properties`) and `attribute_uris`.
3. `src/back/objects/ontology/Ontology.py`: `apply_agent_ontology_changes` applies the same re-derivation and remap before its prune.
4. `src/front/static/global/js/ontology-core.js`: `saveConfigToSession` calls the new `applyStoredUris(result)` after a successful save, so the editor holds the stored URIs (otherwise the next save would send the old URI). Classes and relationships are remapped by old URI, attributes by position.
5. `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js`: comments on the URI carry-over in `saveSharedEntity` and `saveSharedRelationship` updated (the URI is still sent so the backend can identify the item).
6. `docs/user-guide.md`: note that renaming updates the URI and keeps mappings; a build must be re-run for the triples to use the new URI.

Not changed: triples already materialised in the triple store keep the previous URI until the next build; saved artefacts that embed URIs (e.g. SWRL/cohort/simulation results) are not rewritten; relationship constraints/axioms stay name-based as before.

