## Add Sanity Checks Auto-fix (propose-then-apply)

Context: Sanity Checks findings needed a guided repair path. Each fixable finding (and Fix all per rule) now opens a confirmation modal with an explained plan and ranked alternatives. Mechanical rules use deterministic fixers; judgement rules use ``agent_design_fixer``. Orphan attribute attach/remove is folded into this flow (the previous JS-only orphan modal is removed). Apply validates and mutates server-side, remapping URIs/mappings on rename.

Changes:
1. `src/back/objects/ontology/autofix_ops.py`: operation vocabulary, rule routing, naming helpers, FixPlan builders.
2. `src/back/objects/ontology/autofix_rule_fixers.py`: mechanical plans for E01–E05, I02, I03.
3. `src/back/objects/ontology/autofix_apply.py`: atomic apply + attach/remove/rename/merge handlers.
4. `src/back/objects/ontology/DesignAutofix.py`: propose orchestration (rule / AI / No-LLM fallbacks for W02/W03).
5. `src/back/objects/ontology/DesignChecks.py`: DC-E04 findings include ``member`` for Auto-fix.
6. `src/back/objects/ontology/Editor.py`: extract URI rewrite/remap and mapping prune helpers (size budget).
7. `src/agents/agent_design_fixer/`: read-only tools + engine + ``submit_fix_plan`` terminal tool.
8. `src/agents/tools/context.py`: ``ontology_groups`` and ``submitted_fix_plan`` fields.
9. `src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py`: ``POST .../autofix/propose`` and ``.../apply``.
10. `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-design-checks.js`: Auto-fix / Fix all modal; remove orphan modal.
