## Use entity / attribute wording in Sanity Checks and Auto-fix
================================================================================

Context: Sanity Checks titles, messages and the Auto-fix modal used OWL
jargon ("class", "domain", raw op ids like `set_domain` and `domain=Order`).
In OntoBricks the user-facing nouns are entity / attribute / relationship, and
"domain" means an OntoBricks domain, so the rdfs:domain wording was confusing.
Op ids and data fields are unchanged; only user-facing text is renamed.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/ontology/DesignChecks.py
   Rename titles (Broken entity link, Orphan entity, Missing entity, Entity naming, Attribute / relationship naming); reword every finding message to entity / attribute / relationship via new `_noun` / `_plural` helpers.
2. src/back/objects/ontology/autofix_rule_fixers.py
   Reword clear_parent / clear_domain / rename rationales and summaries (no "class" or "domain").
3. src/back/objects/ontology/autofix_apply.py
   Reword apply errors (Entity / Attribute / Relationship not found) via `_prop_noun`.
4. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-design-checks.js
   Mirror the new rule titles; add `OP_LABELS` / `PARAM_LABELS` + `_opLabel` so the modal shows "Set owning entity", "Detach from entity", "entity: Order" instead of raw op ids and `key=value` params.

