## Keep attribute-to-entity membership in sync on set_domain
================================================================================

Context: The Auto-fix operation `set_domain` on an attribute only updated the
attribute's owning entity link, while `attach_attribute` also listed the
attribute under that entity's attributes. Applying `set_domain` therefore left
the attribute missing from its entity's attribute list. `set_domain` now
behaves the same way as `attach_attribute` for attributes. Relationships are
unchanged.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/ontology/autofix_apply.py
   Add `_is_attribute` and `_sync_attribute_owner`; `_op_set_domain` now moves
   the attribute into the target entity's attribute list and removes it from
   the previous entity. Idempotent.
2. tests/units/ontology/test_design_autofix_apply.py
   Add five tests: attach on attribute, move from previous entity, idempotent
   re-apply, relationship left untouched, unknown entity rejected.

Modified files:
- src/back/objects/ontology/autofix_apply.py
- tests/units/ontology/test_design_autofix_apply.py
