## Graph Chat: full, collapsible thinking process
================================================================================

Context: Graph Chat only showed the current tool name in a status line and a
"Tools used" list, with tool results cut to 500 characters on the backend. The
user wants the whole reasoning trace visible in the chat, with expand/collapse.
The trace now shows every tool call (input arguments) and its full result, and
stays on top of the final answer.

Changes:

1. src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/engine.py
   `tool_result` steps carry the full tool output instead of `[:500]`. The LLM
   payload was already untruncated; only the observable step content changes.
2. src/front/static/query/js/query-chat.js
   Streaming bubble builds a collapsible "Thinking process (N tool calls)"
   block, open by default. Each tool call is its own expandable block with
   pretty-printed Input and Result sections and the duration. Blocks fill in
   live as SSE events arrive. The block is kept on success and on error. All
   tool output is rendered via `textContent` (no HTML injection).
3. src/front/static/query/css/query-chat.css
   Styles for `.graph-chat-thinking`, `.graph-chat-step*` (scrollable `pre`,
   dark code panel).
4. tests/units/agents/test_agent_dtwin_chat_engine.py
   New test: a >500-char tool result is kept whole in the trace step.

Limitation: the thinking trace is live-only. It is not persisted with the saved
Graph Chat history, same as the existing "Tools used" list, so it is not shown
again after a page reload.

